        id: 'html-forms-q4',
        question: 'How does the FormData API work and what are its common use cases?',
        answer: 'The FormData API constructs and manipulates key/value pairs representing form fields and their values. It is especially useful for submitting forms via fetch, handling file uploads, and dynamically constructing form payloads.\n\nTo create a FormData from an existing form, pass the form element to the constructor: new FormData(formElement). This captures all named form controls and their current values, including file inputs. You can also create an empty FormData and append entries manually. The difference between append() and set() is that append adds even if the key exists, while set replaces.\n\nFormData provides get(), getAll() (for multi-select or checkbox groups), has(), entries()/keys()/values() iterators, and delete(). For sending via fetch, pass FormData directly as the request body\u2014the browser automatically sets Content-Type to multipart/form-data with the correct boundary. Do not set this header manually.\n\nFor JSON APIs, convert with Object.fromEntries(formData), but note this only captures the first value for each key. For multi-value fields, iterate manually.\n\nFormData is also useful for modifying submissions. The "formdata" event on a form element fires just before submission, allowing you to add computed values, CSRF tokens, or metadata without hidden inputs.',
        shortAnswer: 'FormData constructs key/value pairs from form fields for programmatic submission via fetch or XMLHttpRequest. It handles file uploads, supports append/set/get/delete operations, and automatically sets the correct multipart Content-Type. Use Object.fromEntries(formData) for JSON conversion.',
        code: 'const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>(\'#uploadForm\');\nform?.addEventListener(\'submit\', async (e: Event) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const formData = new FormData(form);\n  formData.append(\'timestamp\', Date.now().toString());\n\n  // Multipart upload\n  const response = await fetch(\'/api/upload\', {\n    method: \'POST\',\n    body: formData, // Do NOT set Content-Type header\n  });\n\n  // JSON submission\n  const jsonData = Object.fromEntries(formData);\n  await fetch(\'/api/data\', {\n    method: \'POST\',\n    headers: { \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(jsonData),\n  });\n});',
