        id: 'html-apis-q4',
        question: 'What are localStorage and sessionStorage, and what are their limitations?',
        answer: 'Both Web Storage APIs provide key-value storage with a synchronous API: setItem, getItem, removeItem, clear, and length. They store string data only.\n\nlocalStorage persists indefinitely across sessions, shared across all tabs and windows of the same origin. sessionStorage is scoped to a single tab session\u2014it persists through reloads but is cleared when the tab closes. Duplicate tabs get independent copies.\n\nBoth have a ~5-10 MB limit per origin and require JSON.stringify/parse for objects. Exceeding the quota throws QuotaExceededError that must be caught.\n\nKey limitations: the synchronous API blocks the main thread during operations, making it unsuitable for large data. There is no built-in expiration mechanism. It is inaccessible from web workers or service workers. For complex data needs, IndexedDB is better.\n\nSecurity is important: Web Storage is accessible to any JavaScript on the same origin, including XSS payloads. Never store sensitive data like tokens without understanding the risk. The storage event fires on other tabs of the same origin when localStorage changes, enabling basic cross-tab communication.',
        shortAnswer: 'localStorage persists indefinitely across sessions; sessionStorage is scoped to a single tab. Both store strings only (~5-10 MB limit) with a synchronous API. Key limitations: blocks main thread, no expiration, no indexing, and vulnerable to XSS.',
        code: 'localStorage.setItem(\'user\', JSON.stringify({ name: \'Alice\' }));\nconst raw = localStorage.getItem(\'user\');\nconst user = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) as { name: string } : null;\n\n// Storage with expiration pattern\nfunction setWithExpiry(key: string, value: unknown, ttlMs: number): void {\n  const item = { value, expiry: Date.now() + ttlMs };\n  localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(item));\n}\n\nfunction getWithExpiry<T>(key: string): T | null {\n  const raw = localStorage.getItem(key);\n  if (!raw) return null;\n  const item = JSON.parse(raw) as { value: T; expiry: number };\n  if (Date.now() > item.expiry) {\n    localStorage.removeItem(key);\n    return null;\n  }\n  return item.value;\n}\n\n// Cross-tab communication\nwindow.addEventListener(\'storage\', (e: StorageEvent) => {\n  if (e.key === \'theme\' && e.newValue) {\n    document.body.className = e.newValue;\n  }\n});',
