        answer: 'Testing involves multiple tools catching different issues. Schema.org Markup Validator parses your page and shows extracted items, validating syntax correctness and schema compliance.\n\nGoogle Rich Results Test checks if structured data is eligible for Google rich results, showing detected types, errors, warnings, and previews. It applies Google-specific rules stricter than the schema.org specification.\n\nGoogle Search Console provides ongoing monitoring. The "Enhancements" section shows structured data across your site, reporting errors, warnings, and valid items. It tracks impressions and clicks for pages with rich results.\n\nBrowser extensions like "Structured Data Testing Tool" visualize microdata on live pages. Programmatic testing with microdata-parsing libraries enables automated CI/CD testing to prevent regressions.\n\nBest practices: validate during development, not just after deployment. Test with both Google and other search engine tools. Check that structured data matches visible content. Monitor Search Console regularly. Set up automated tests for critical structured data.',
