        answer: 'JSON-LD encodes structured data as JSON within <script type="application/ld+json">. It is Google-recommended because it cleanly separates machine-readable data from HTML markup.\n\nThe structure uses @context (always "https://schema.org"), @type (the schema type), and @id (unique entity identifier). Properties use camelCase names from schema.org.\n\nJSON-LD advantages: decoupled from HTML (change layout without affecting data), standard JSON (easy server-side generation), natural nesting for complex relationships, and support for multiple entities via separate blocks or @id references.\n\nYou can include multiple JSON-LD blocks per page, each describing different aspects. Dynamic SPAs can inject or update blocks programmatically\u2014Google parses dynamically generated JSON-LD.\n\nJSON-LD data and visible content should stay synchronized. Google has flagged cases where JSON-LD contained fabricated claims. The structured data should accurately reflect what users see on the page.',
